>and fell through a trap, which separated me from my pet.  (Which is a 
>bad thing)  Currently, I'm searching for the stairs up to get back to my 
>pet.  (Assuming she doesn't die while I'm gone.)

Most likely she won't. First off in Nethack, levels that the player are not
on exists in a kind of stasis. There's no active monster movement, or
fighting. Time still ticks though. If you are gone way to long, then your
pet will lose its tameness due to being hungry.

>  If she does, I'll be sad... but at least I have that handy (blessed) 
> Scroll of Taming to get a new pet. 

That's a real powerful scroll. I advise saving it for a really good pet
or a really tough monster.

You can tame ordinary domesticated pets (dogs, cats, horses) by feeding
them. You can get them to become  peaceful and stop attacking you by 
throwing any type of food item whether they eat it or not.

> So, my second question is:  What sorts of creatures will a 
>scroll of taming work on?

Virtually everything. Note that high level monsters are resistance to
magic. So you may not be able to tame them.

Again I'd suggest keeping it stuck in your back pocket until you get into
a tight spot or come across a really good wild monster that you can tame.

